{
 "about": "slice 13's hand-over to the orlop slice (14): the berth deck's line, its beams' stations and sizes, and what passes through it. Metres in the ship's frame (x forward, y to starboard, z up, z = 0 at waterline A); sizes in inches where the name ends _in. Written Nov 17 2026 from the gun deck as built at 4e131bd4 (slice 12), revised the same day for the ladderways (revised); slice 13's build will write the same fields to build.json and this file will be kept current until it merges.",
 "sources": "the 1926 midship section (NARA, the orlop slice's reading): the berth deck's top 7 ft 2 in under the gun deck's top. The 1795 midship section drawn from Humphreys' specifications (NARA 75841360, measured at 4.0 px an inch from its keel's 18 by 24 in): lower deck plank to gun deck plank 6 ft 4 in on a gun deck 23 ft 3 in over the rabbet, the lower deck about 17 ft over it; our gun deck stands 7.37 m (24 ft 2 in) over the rabbet (the 1927 lines' port sills less 24 in), so 7 ft 2 in under it puts our berth deck 17 ft over the rabbet amidships, where the 1795 section has it (the 10 in more between our decks is our gun deck standing higher). Its beams: 14 in moulded (written '14 x 1?', the second figure unclear; 14 3/4 in drawn) and its planks 3 1/2 in yellow pine; the gun deck's beams '15 x 18' (15 in drawn deep). Read as moulded by sided",
